6.1.5.m:
'May the divine waters be for our aid, / may they be for our drinking;

may they flow blessings and peace upon us.'

'May the waters of the desert be auspicious to us, / may those of the marshland be auspicious to us;

may the ocean waters be auspicious to us, / and may the well-waters be auspicious to us.'

'May Mitra be auspicious to us, may Varuṇa be auspicious, / may Aryaman be auspicious to us;

may Indra and Agni be auspicious to us, / may wide-striding Viṣṇu be auspicious to us.'

With these three verses, they purify themselves beyond the cowpen.

6.2.6.m:
"Suck this honeyed breast of the waters, / swollen, Agni, in the midst of the flood;

Enjoy the spring, the honeyed wave; / enter the oceanic flood!"

—with this, he mutters the unyoking of the fire.
